{"name":"Meltwater","hex":"#79c0cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"meltwater","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water from melting ice or snow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meltwater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meltwater","blocks":[{"text":"Meltwater is water released by the melting of snow or ice, including glacial ice, tabular icebergs and ice shelves over oceans. Meltwater is often found during early spring when snow packs and frozen rivers melt with rising temperatures, and in the ablation zone of glaciers where the rate of snow cover is reducing. Meltwater can be produced during volcanic eruptions, in a similar way in which the more dangerous lahars form. It can also be produced by the heat generated by the flow itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Kinney_Run_looking_downstream_in_Spring_2015.JPG/330px-Kinney_Run_looking_downstream_in_Spring_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meltwater","wikidata":"Q360925"},{"title":"Meltwater (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Meltwater is an online media, social and consumer intelligence company. The company was founded in Oslo, Norway, by Jørn Lyseggen, in 2001 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California, with additional offices across Europe, North America, Asia/Pacific, Australia, and Africa. The company employs around 2,200 people and has approximately 27,000 clients internationally. In February 2023, Meltwater reported US$439 million in revenue for the full 2022 fiscal year."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meltwater_(company)","wikidata":"Q1142400"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Cavell_Glacier_with_Crevices_and_Annual_Rings.jpg/500px-Cavell_Glacier_with_Crevices_and_Annual_Rings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Cavell_Glacier_with_Crevices_and_Annual_Rings.jpg/1280px-Cavell_Glacier_with_Crevices_and_Annual_Rings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Cavell_Glacier_with_Crevices_and_Annual_Rings.jpg/500px-Cavell_Glacier_with_Crevices_and_Annual_Rings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Meltwater from Mount Edith Cavell Cavell Glacier","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACavell_Glacier_with_Crevices_and_Annual_Rings.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Meltwater_MOSAiC.jpg/500px-Meltwater_MOSAiC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Meltwater_MOSAiC.jpg/1280px-Meltwater_MOSAiC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Meltwater_MOSAiC.jpg/500px-Meltwater_MOSAiC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Meltwater transfer from sea ice surface melt ponds to the ocean during MOSAiC Expedition ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeltwater_MOSAiC.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Fryxellsee_Opt.jpg/500px-Fryxellsee_Opt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Fryxellsee_Opt.jpg/1280px-Fryxellsee_Opt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Fryxellsee_Opt.jpg/500px-Fryxellsee_Opt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Refrozen glacial meltwater from the Canada Glacier, in Antarctica","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFryxellsee_Opt.jpg"},{"